Mages now learn Mage Sight, a new sorcery spell that consolidates
several vision buffs into a single cast.

Mage sight provides a direct vision bonus and can passively grant
infravision, detect invisible, true sight, detect magic, and sense
life based on your skill in each. These passives are applied
automatically when you cast mage sight -- no need to cast them
individually. The passives rise and fall with the primary spell:
dispelling or expiring mage sight removes all of its passives.

Mage sight can also be cast on a group target to buff your entire 
party at once by casting without a target specified.

The individual vision spells still exist on potions and scrolls. 
